        },
        "text_waGfLw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The Cedar Bucket, located on Highway 6, serves as a cherished landmark and the gateway to Oxford. Proudly recognized as the world’s largest cedar bucket, it was originally built in 1985 by the previous owner, whose craftsmanship and vision brought this unique structure to life. Preserved as a piece of local history, the Cedar Bucket stands as a testament to the area’s heritage and invites visitors to experience its grandeur firsthand.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "sb_custom_font": "Neutra Text Book",
